\begin{description}
\item[* name:] RPasClauseFormation
\item[* relevant examples:] be considered he a fool by x1, be quickly turned 
on the radio by she, $^{*}$[I had] be built a house by EMPTY 
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) english
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] XPPropTOClause
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) RC\_
ClauseFormation
\item[* date of creation:] 5-FEB-1988 
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] RActClauseFormation
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] generate a top  category that can later be specified for time 
attributes etc. and introduce the auxiliary of the passive
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:]
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\
It is assumed that the (incorrect) sentence {\em [I had] the house be built by 
him\/} is indeed generated, but will be filtered out later. The correct version 
is generated in the VERBPPROPtoFORMULA subgrammar, where no auxiliary is added.
\end{enumerate}
